From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Nothing closing is nothing to keep

0069's wouldLeaveTheScreenEmpty() asks whether the applications that are
opening have anything on the screen, and when none does it says the previous
screen is to be kept. It did not ask whether there was a previous screen to
keep: with mClosingApps empty the answer was still "keep", the log said
"keeping 0 screen(s)" (on the device, 2026-11-03), and the loop that holds the
closing applications turned zero times. Harmless in effect, and wrong in what
it said -- and that line is the one judge of this branch in every device run
since (patches/VERIFICATION.md), so a judge that can say something false is a
defect of its own. Issue #2 (a) in the public repository; open-items, "two
small changes, first in line for the next image".

What changes: when nothing is closing the question is answered "no" before the
opening applications are looked at. The other half of Issue #2, writing
ro.pw3.hold_screen_past_deadline into pw3.mk so that the property list says
the feature is on, is in device/amazon/pw3 and not here.

Not run on the device yet when this patch was written. What to watch for: a
transition past its deadline with nothing closing logs nothing from this
branch; the X1-X7 runs of 2026-11-04 (section 3a of the takeover notes) are
unchanged, since every one of them had a closing application.

